---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/13-08/', specs='https://www.leica-microsystems.com/products/sample-preparation-for-electron-microscopy/p/leica-em-ice/specification/', product='https://www.leica-microsystems.com/fileadmin/global/products/Nano/Leica-EM-ICE-HP-Freezer.jpg', installed='https://medresearch.umich.edu/sites/default/files/styles/wide/public/2023-08/res_micro_core_Leica%20EM%20ICE%20High%20Pressure%20Freezer.jpg.jpg?itok=sDX8QgQI';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Leica EM ICE · sealed exterior and detached annotation" description="Inspect a dormant Leica EM ICE exterior and annotate the dimensions of an unrelated synthetic tile." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ice"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-08/">← Equipment 13-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ice-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">13-08 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & DETACHED EXHIBIT / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Leica EM ICE</h2><p>Orbit the sealed, unpowered instrument. On the separate teaching stand, compare two simple metal-tile outlines and record their geometry without changing the originals. The tiles are not instrument accessories or specimens.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Dormant exterior and separate exhibit</h3><div id="ice-view" aria-label="Orbitable Leica EM ICE exterior with blank panel and an independent nearby tile exhibit"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-ice-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-ice-view="shell">Exterior detail</button><button data-ice-view="exhibit">Detached exhibit</button><button id="ice-cycle">Switch detached tile</button></div>
<p id="ice-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge sits on the independent exhibit and switches highlighted tiles only. The device has no available actions.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached outline annotation</h3><canvas id="ice-plot" width="700" height="440" aria-label="Authored rectangular tile outline, orthogonal edge lengths and diagonal at a common scale"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Exhibit tile<select id="ice-tile"><option value="TILE-A">A · 60 × 80 mm</option><option value="TILE-B">B · 120 × 50 mm</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="ice-annotate">Record outline annotation</button><button id="ice-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="ice-status" aria-live="polite">Select one of the two detached tiles and record its outline.</p><output id="ice-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="ice-json" disabled>Annotation JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="ice-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: standard Leica EM ICE main body and working station with the M80 exterior silhouette, as shown in the <a href={product}>Leica whole-instrument photograph</a>. The <a href={installed}>University of Michigan installed equipment photo</a> establishes the stepped case, black work surface, opaque cover and inactive tilted display appearance. <a href={specs}>Leica published dimensions</a> anchor the overall body and workstation size; component sizes and trim are visually inferred. The user-facing panel is blank and all hardware remains sealed.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original whole exterior render, with wheeled pale body and a detached exhibit nearby"/><figcaption>Original whole-instrument render, not a photograph. Compared with the manufacturer front quarter view for proportions and visible casters.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original exterior detail with black work surface, blank screen and cosmetic red cover"/><figcaption>Original detail compared with the installed front photo. The visible cover and fixed M80 housing are represented only by solid silhouettes.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Main body and station</td><td>1,160 W × 790 D × 1,285 H mm</td><td>Metric GLB envelope, reproduced to 0.01 mm export tolerance; no internal tolerances inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tile A outline</td><td>60 × 80 mm, ideal diagonal 100 mm</td><td>100 mm from authored endpoints; unrelated to instrument fit.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tile B outline</td><td>120 × 50 mm, ideal diagonal 130 mm</td><td>130 mm from authored endpoints; separately revisioned.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reference register acceptance</td><td>Preservation metadata on a labeled specimen</td><td>Not implemented or run. This is annotation-only on detached inert tiles, with immutable coordinates and unknown interior.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Each tile has an authored local frame with +X to the right and +Y up, in millimeters. An annotation reads edge and diagonal lengths using <code>√[(x₂−x₁)²+(y₂−y₁)²]</code>. JSON preserves the corners, source geometry revision and previous annotation per tile. The output makes no claims about the interior or material. There are no cooling/pressure parameters, operational controls, biological inputs, freezing, setup or handling procedures.</p>
<p><a href={base+'leica-em-ice-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'outline-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-08/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ice{max-width:76rem}.ice .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.ice section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.ice .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.ice .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.ice label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.ice input,.ice select,.ice button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.ice button{cursor:pointer}.ice button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.ice .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.ice #ice-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.ice #ice-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ice #ice-plot,.ice img{width:100%;height:auto}.ice #ice-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.ice #ice-status.error{color:#a54a34}.ice .scroll{overflow:auto}.ice table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.ice td,.ice th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.ice figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.ice .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
